  "question": {
    "text": "To increase the resonant frequency in series LCR circuit,",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "U9BUj",
      "text": "Source frequency should be increased",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "99oGE",
      "text": "Another resistance should be added in series with the first resistance.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cfCBx",
      "text": "Another capacitor should be added in series with the first capacitor",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "1gloZ",
      "text": "The source frequency should be decreased",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The resonant frequency of an LCR circuit is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mi>L</mi><mi>C</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>. It does not depend on the source frequency as well as the resistance of the circuit.</p><p>Therefore, to increase the resonating frequency product of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> should decrease.</p><p>By joining another capacitor in series, the equivalent capacitor will decrease.</p><p>Hence, option C is correct option.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
